{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "007X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}^\\# \\to \\mathcal{G}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-sheafify-universal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:baf83076fb3497687822002999fe874ae25530a82bd3658ceeb766389bd9dec8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fad1f816bac0c4b3980f67d60756c32daf8d9d47c3d675e4efa82375a05c7d47", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a presheaf of sets on <MATH_0002>.\nAny map <MATH_0003> into a sheaf of sets\nfactors uniquely as\n<MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6b72bc0bfbe0177aa071d641343f10e766a6b193422aa23a51e0db4ad275cae8", "unit_id": "tag:0080:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "007X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F} \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\mathcal{F}^\\# \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\Pi(\\mathcal{F}) \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{G} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{G}^\\# \\ar[r] &\n\\Pi(\\mathcal{G}) \\\\\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{G} = \\mathcal{G}^\\#$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}_x \\to \\mathcal{G}^\\#_x$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-points-exactness}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-stalk-sheafification}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a6456f848967589a44843276cd9f22b69f4028fb2f0e714d36f271507f633a2b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:77eeb2a6e97dfe299ee80b7c077c31cd14816b842219b2c18f31832d50018f4e", "source_text": "Clearly, there is a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nSo it suffices to prove that <MATH_0002>.\nTo see this it suffices to prove, for every point <MATH_0003> the\nmap <MATH_0004> is bijective, by\nLemma <REF_0001>. And this is\nLemma <REF_0002> above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8314a6cb27c8602313a218275b918cad1fe68585d23b6dbd81743a69ca1735ce", "unit_id": "tag:0080:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "007X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : \\Sh(X) \\to \\textit{PSh}(X)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\# : \\textit{PSh}(X) \\to \\Sh(X)$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(X)}(\\mathcal{F}, i(\\mathcal{G}))\n=\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(X)}(\\mathcal{F}^\\#, \\mathcal{G})\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-section-adjoint}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ac32f14b41207a20e1be9c8d900c77eb3d9d213e7dfd4db6d8905326298d2cfb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:18b3c9230d77ab143e03ef032434fb4bc9353cbd0a504f54fcdf761dd8cc8d66", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis lemma really says that there is an adjoint pair\nof functors: <MATH_0001>\n(inclusion) and <MATH_0002>\n(sheafification). The formula is that\n<MATH_0003>\nwhich says that sheafification is a left adjoint of\nthe inclusion functor. See Categories, Section\n<REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:54f9d1852562f37dc083a472dadf9b7ac929ddae7cfc1e4539b905277ebf610a", "unit_id": "tag:007X:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "007X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A_p \\to \\underline{A}$", "MATH_0002": "$A_p^\\# \\to \\underline{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "MATH_0004": "$A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-stalk-constant-presheaf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-sheafify-constant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ff43a5f88c7ca7de638821e266ea8c727408d5e5e7bba30e04228513d4df8227", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ab3aef178eb2904e8dc5538fcd7a41b43ac7eefad585d82aff54b521180199f9", "source_text": "See Example <REF_0001> for notation.\nThe map <MATH_0001> induces a map\n<MATH_0002>. It is easy to see that this\nis an isomorphism. In words: The sheafification\nof the constant presheaf with value <MATH_0003> is the\nconstant sheaf with value <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:73d561b56ead8d5587381171d5290a249e62e40efc4b9264226cb3e2fd8ea6a0", "unit_id": "tag:0081:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "007X", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}^\\#$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-separated-presheaf-into-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:be18bf5df24730690af31dae10dd7aa058c9756967ade45bf884fd35ae64f478", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e4e31532df5552d068a44d2227bc0470d6ce6063d92c5499b5f7f2a4cc65382e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a topological space.\nA presheaf <MATH_0002> is separated (see\nDefinition <REF_0001>) if and only if\nthe canonical map <MATH_0003> is injective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6524bd9d60668a23cf1059a4b75a723782df311a9e018d061d778a9080fc1161", "unit_id": "tag:0082:statement"}
